WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:06.410
Scar is one of Disney's most memorable villains,
but the 2019 Lion King movie has changed some

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.809
crucial details about the evil lion's origins
and story.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:14.549
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining the new secret history

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:17.210
of Scar that's revealed in The Lion King remake.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:22.009
Plus I'll tell you how the new movie addresses
a long-standing fan theory that Scar and Mufasa

00:00:22.009 --> 00:00:23.500
aren't actually brothers.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.830
Some spoilers, so take care if you haven't
seen it yet.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.779
Don't forget my giveaway is running, so be
sure to subscribe and let me know your thoughts

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:33.140
about Scar for a chance to win.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:37.520
The origin of Scar's name and how he received
the wound on his eye were never addressed

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.800
in the classic movie.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.930
However, there's a vital addition to the remake's
version of the following scene:

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.110
"Perhaps you shouldn't turn your back on me."

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:48.489
"Is that a challenge?"

00:00:48.489 --> 00:00:50.129
"Temper, temper.

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:53.500
I wouldn't dream of challenging you."

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:59.469
In the 2019 version, Scar says "I wouldn't
dream of challenging you again" meaning that

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:03.050
there's already been a confrontation between
the two lions in the past.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:08.140
And I think the new film hints that it was
during this previous challenge that Mufasa

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.340
gave Scar the signature wound across his left
eye.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:16.720
For example, in the reworked story, when Mufasa
begs his brother for help during the stampede,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.189
Scar viciously slashes him across the eye
which sends Mufasa plunging to his death in

00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:22.189
the gorge below.

00:01:22.189 --> 00:01:27.450
This is a change to the traditional animation
where Scar flings Mufasa off the cliff.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.799
By adding the face slash in the remake, it
suggests that the villainous lion is taking

00:01:31.799 --> 00:01:35.140
revenge in kind for the scar Mufasa gave him.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.730
Now, what's also interesting about this change
is that it seems to invalidate the backstory

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:43.620
given to Scar in a book series that was a
spin-off from the classic film.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.329
The first story of that series, "A Tale of
Two Brothers", recounted that Scar was originally

00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:53.290
called Taka and that he changed his name to
Scar after getting into a scrape with a buffalo

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.820
that slashed him across the eye with his horns.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.369
Although that book series was authorised by
Disney, it's not entirely clear whether it's

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:04.970
ever been canon as elements from it don't
fit with the animated Lion King sequel.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:11.610
Either way the 2019 movie suggests a brand
new origin for Scar's signature wound.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.690
Another change in the remake that's quite
likely related to that fateful challenge between

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:21.051
Scar and Mufasa is Scar's new backstory with
Sarabi, who was Mufasa's queen of the Pride

00:02:21.051 --> 00:02:22.051
Lands.

00:02:22.051 --> 00:02:26.950
In the new movie, a subplot involving romantic
jealousy has been added to Scar's origins,

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:31.640
and the first hint comes at the beginning
of the new story when Scar says to Mufasa

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:36.300
and Zazu, "As you know I have tremendous respect
for the queen."

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:41.080
In fact, in the novelization of the new Lion
King film, when Scar says that line it triggers

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.380
an intense anger in Mufasa.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:48.660
This indicates that Mufasa and Scar's rivalry
over Sarabi has been stewing for some time.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:52.970
And it also reveals that, as well as wanting
to rule the Pride Lands, there was an additional

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:56.380
motive behind Scar's personal feud with Mufasa.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:01.920
Later, after Scar takes over as king, Sarabi
accuses him of overhunting, at which point

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:07.550
he reveals "long ago you chose Mufasa over
me, but now there is a new king."

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:12.090
With Mufasa gone, Scar now requests that she
join him as queen.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:17.060
That new dialogue reminds me of a deleted
scene from the 1994 movie where Scar was wondering

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.900
why his subjects don't look up to him like
they did his brother:

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:21.900
"I'm sick to death of him.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.640
What did he have that I don't have?"

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:31.120
"Adoring subjects, respect of your species,
a loving family, a devoted queen, shall I

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.440
go on sire?"

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:37.270
In the remake, Scar realises that he's unloved
by the rest of the pride and believes that,

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:42.190
if he can make Sarabi his partner, then he'll
gain the respect she has from the other lions.

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.990
"Yes I need a queen.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.560
She would rule by side.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:49.070
We'll have cubs, little Scars running all
over the place."

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:54.990
In the deleted scene from 1994, Scar actually
proposes to Nala rather than Sarabi.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:59.800
Like Simba's mother, Nala also refused, and
Scar responded by threatening her.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:00.800
"Nala, Nala, Nala..

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:01.800
You know you really have no choice.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:08.350
One way or another I always get what I want.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:12.570
Either be my queen or be forever banished
from the Pride Lands."

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:16.310
Scar's creepy threats in the animated movie
were also going to be one of the reasons that

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.310
Nala decided to leave Pride Rock to look for
help.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:24.010
And there's another nod to that deleted scene
in a brand new scene for Nala in the remake,

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:28.630
where she has to sneak around Scar and the
hyenas before she can get away.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:32.530
Another change to Scar's backstory is that
in the new version, he doesn't team up with

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:35.730
the hyenas before his visit to the elephant
graveyard.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:40.130
Now when Scar arrives, it's clear there isn't
an alliance between them yet as they even

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.530
threaten to eat him.

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:45.540
This is quite different to the first movie
where the hyenas are obviously on familiar

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:46.870
terms with Scar.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.440
"Oh Scar, it's just you."

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.070
"We were afraid it was somebody important."

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.070
"I mean, you're one of us.

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:53.250
I mean, you're our pal."

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.210
He even brings them fresh meat to eat.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.710
"I don't think you really deserve this.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:01.170
I practically gift-wrapped those cubs for
you."

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:05.450
Given Scar's lack of familiarity with the
hyenas in the CG reboot, it seems like his

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:10.280
plan to send Simba to the elephant graveyard
wasn't something pre-arranged with them.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.500
He was simply hoping to take advantage of
the hyenas' natural behaviour and that they'd

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.110
kill and eat the young cub of their own accord.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:21.720
There's an interesting change to how Scar
guilt-trips Simba about Mufasa's death in

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:22.730
the remake.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:27.640
This time Scar takes Simba into the gorge
specifically under the pretext that the little

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.530
cub needs to practise his roar.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:34.280
"This gorge is where all lions come to find
their roar."

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:36.120
"Watch this!"

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.230
"You'll get it Simba.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.230
Just takes time."

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.700
"Dad will be so proud, won't he?"

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.420
"It's a gift he'll never forget."

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:49.000
By contrast, in the 1994 classic, Scar tells
Simba to wait there for a "marvellous surprise"

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.000
from his father.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.000
"Oooh, What is it?"

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.690
"If I told you, it wouldn't be a surprise
now, would it?"

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:59.770
and, rather deviously, only mentions practising
his roar as a throwaway line, in passing.

00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:05.180
"And just between us, you might want to work
on that little roar of yours, hmm?"

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:10.660
However, in the new movie, Scar deliberately
and clearly links Simba's roar with his father.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.870
"Even Mufasa came here when he was your age.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:18.930
Refused to leave until his roar could be heard
above the rim."

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:23.430
Which firmly plants the seed in the young
lion's mind that practising his roar led to

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:24.710
his dad's death.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:29.740
That makes Simba feel even guiltier later
when he thinks his father died trying to save

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:30.740
him.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:34.880
And when Scar arrives to find the poor little
cub grieving over his dead father, in the

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:39.300
remake the villain twists the knife even further
with some brand new lines that weren't in

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.070
the animated movie.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:45.750
Scar says to Simba, "Your father had such
hopes for you, gave you so many chances.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.520
And this is how you repay him."

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:50.980
Then after asking the young cub "What will
your mother think?",

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:53.910
in the new version, Scar also tells Simba,
he's

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:56.110
"A son who causes his father's death.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:58.810
A boy who kills a king."

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:03.341
Something that's confused Lion King fans for
many years is a theory that claims Scar and

00:07:03.341 --> 00:07:05.530
Mufasa might not really be brothers.

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:10.200
I think the new movie gives its own answer
to that question, but just before we get into

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:15.330
that, we need to review the evidence for why
Scar and Mufasa might not be related by blood.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:20.750
The moment from the 1994 movie used to support
that theory is when Scar compares his intellectual

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.900
and physical capabilities with Mufasa's.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:26.200
"Well, as far as brains go, I got the lion's
share.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:33.540
But when it comes to brute strength, I'm afraid
I'm at the shallow end of the gene pool."

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:38.490
The theory claims that what Scar's really
saying is that he and Mufasa aren't genetically

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:39.490
related.

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:42.770
When it comes to the theory, there have been
some conflicting attempts by the animation's

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:44.500
filmmakers to clarify the situation.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:50.871
In a 2017 interview with Hello Giggles, producer
Don Hahn said, "[While making the movie] we

00:07:50.871 --> 00:07:55.290
talked about the fact that it was very likely
[Scar and Mufasa] would not have both the

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.560
same parents.

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.570
Occasionally there are prides that do have
two male lions, [but] they're not equals.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:03.680
One lion will always kind of be off in the
shadows.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:08.730
We were trying to use those animal truths
to underpin the story so we sort of figured

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:12.520
Scar and Mufasa couldn't really be from the
same gene pool."

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:17.470
But while Hahn heavily implied Scar and Mufasa
weren't brothers, to add to the confusion,

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:22.820
a couple of weeks later, The Lion King's director
Rob Minkoff told Screen Junkies the exact

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:28.490
opposite, saying that he wanted to clear up
that Scar and Mufasa were in fact brothers.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:33.409
Despite all that, the 2019 movie seems to
take a few steps to provide more clarity.

00:08:33.409 --> 00:08:38.479
First of all, Scar's "shallow end of the gene
pool" line has been replaced

00:08:38.479 --> 00:08:43.890
and he now says "when it comes to brute strength,
I'm afraid my big brother will always rule."

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:48.300
So, the original line which seemed to trigger
the theory has been scrapped and substituted

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.890
with Scar specifically calling Mufasa his
"big brother".

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:55.160
On top of that, there's another change at
the end of the new film.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:59.720
Just after Scar confesses to Simba that he
killed Mufasa, a new line has been added where

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:03.430
Simba asks him, "your own brother, how could
you?"

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:07.690
The emphasis on this new line implies that
Simba is completely outraged because he views

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:12.540
Scar's murder of Mufasa as even more heinous
as the two lions were related.

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:16.850
Disney also used the opportunity of remaking
The Lion King to fix a number of other mistakes

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:19.040
and confusing moments in the classic movie.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:21.640
You can learn all about those in my other
video.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:24.930
Tap the screen to watch that or click the
link in the video description.

